WEBVTT

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:02.840
And that's why,

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:03.900
on a temporary basis,

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.360
<i>I</i> have been entrusted with 
protecting this village.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.640
Who is he?

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.370
The Headmaster's servant.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.260
Um, Mr. Headmaster's Servant?

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.740
Holdem. Chief of Security. Super capable.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.750
Mr. Super-Capable Chief of Security Holdem,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.750
in the last test I got pretty darn hurt.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.380
Are you here to do awful 
stuff again this time?

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.480
My purpose here is to inspect the village.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.140
I just happened to have this foisted on me

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.140
because I'm capable.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.990
He's awfully insistent about that.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:42.890
Is he actually capable?

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.520
He's known for his nasty personality.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.690
You're an unendearing bunch!

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:52.400
Okay, announcement over. 
Now scram. Scram! Go!

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.520
Ugh, kids.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:55.240
So,

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:59.120
why art thou really here?

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:05.010
Just as a Remnant of Disaster appears, 
thou showest up to inspect.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.280
It hardly seems unrelated.

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:09.380
It <i>is</i> unrelated.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:12.710
If I used a Remnant of Disaster, 
the village would fall.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:14.840
I shall believe thee.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.060
About that Remnant problem...

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.240
Can you take care of it?

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.850
"Take care of it?"

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:25.600
The one thing I appreciate 
about you is your skills.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:29.230
You're the sole witch my master relied on.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:35.740
Well, Sorena was my friend, after all...

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:47.270
Sorena died protecting people.
 She would ask me to protect the village.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.500
As for compensation?

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.880
Access to <i>The Grimoire of Zero</i>.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:56.500
What?!

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.510
Please, Loux. I swear, I'll persuade my lady.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.260
This village is her dream.

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:06.230
We'll do anything to protect it.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:11.230
Even trust me? I see!

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:44.700
Huh? You want to get stronger?

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:50.040
Episode 8          Respective Costs

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:50.040
Yeah. Today I decided I want to 
be a proper mage like you two.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:54.540
Of course! Let's graduate together 
and become mages together!

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:59.100
But... I don't think I'll be able 
to keep doing the chores like I was.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.150
Like the laundry...

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:07.390
Like I said before! You don't 
have to wash... my clothes!

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:11.320
Hurry home, you three.

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:12.940
O-Oh...

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.160
Professor Los?

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:16.190
No need for concern.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.940
You better be okay...

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:22.670
I'd still lose some sleep if you died.

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:38.630
So... what I wanted to ask... is...

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:41.780
I want you two to teach me to cast.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.620
In exchange, I'll restore your magic.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.910
Sounds fine to me.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:51.520
Actually, I thought it was nuts that 
you didn't ask for anything before.

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:56.020
To be honest, I felt like we 
leaned on you a little too much.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:57.900
Wh-While we're on the subject,

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.200
I was curious about something...

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:07.560
Sayb, sometimes you... supply 
magic through your l-lips, right?

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:14.040
So, um, like! Does that mean 
you might do that with me?

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.670
Huh? No, I don't think so.

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:21.690
Y-You won't, huh? I see!

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:26.680
I'm surprised you're unfazed by it, dude.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.050
By what?

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.850
Think about it with the genders swapped.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.560
Gender... swap?

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:38.940
I want to devour you.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.570
This is the difference experience makes.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:48.070
I don't really see an issue.

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:50.120
You can't do that!

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.200
It's against morality!

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.080
A mortal sin!

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:56.210
I won't let that happen to my Saybina!

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.470
"Saybina"?

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:58.580
"My"?

00:05:58.580 --> 00:05:59.560
Hey.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:04.090
Can you show me to an empty 
house where I can rest?

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.120
Sure. I'll take you.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:08.050
That won't do.

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:12.040
I can't go to an empty house 
alone with a young maiden.

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:14.470
The village's population will increase.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:18.780
What a creep!

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:21.500
We should file a complaint 
with the Headmaster.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:23.020
I-I'm sorry!

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:24.980
Please! Just don't tell my lady!

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:25.860
Saybil.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.660
Mr. Uls...

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.300
We need to talk.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:35.120
I-In that case, we'll take Mr. Holdem.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.870
I know it's not your fault.

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:44.280
Laios cried and defended you.

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:45.880
Sir, I...

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:47.940
Still, I'm sorry,

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:51.760
but I need you to stay away from our son.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.280
Yes, sir.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.320
Do you want to go out with 
me while I practice magic?

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:10.530
So, you'll practice magic with me every day?

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:18.870
Once I'm strong enough to protect him, 
may I take him out again?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:24.020
I promised him we'd play adventurers again.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:27.180
It's just a promise to a kid.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.420
But we're friends.

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:40.140
I'll teach Laios a little more about 
staying safe in the forest by then.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:46.140
Careless of ya.

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:51.620
To be alone at night like this.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:07.710
Yet another person you love 
is gonna die because of you.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:10.470
How long are you gonna repress it?

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:16.760
Listen closely, dear.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:21.180
You must <i>never</i> approach a 
witch who has eyes like yours.

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:23.730
Mom...

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:26.470
She'll take everything from you.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.130
Hid him in a barrier, eh?

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:53.890
Come out, child.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.890
If you don't want to let your mom die.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.360
Come on.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:07.770
Mom!

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.100
Now, come along.

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:30.540
Show me.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:42.220
Ah, the power! Just the 
slightest touch and I feel it.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:43.310
Yes!

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:44.560
<i>This</i> is...

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:53.820
Stop!

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:56.320
Let go of me!

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:23.340
Hey!

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:29.260
Spare me all that.

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:32.960
My orders were to take
 you alive this time.

00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:37.100
Um, am I being abducted?

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:40.200
What does it look like?

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:45.990
Um, I think I'll probably be a 
disappointment to your employer.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.640
Not my problem.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:51.280
I'm a tool. I just get used for my purpose.

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:55.000
Damn. Someone's caught up to us.

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:58.380
Hey! You said you could drive the horses!

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:02.650
I <i>am</i> driving them! They're flying 
forward, aren't they? See?

00:11:02.650 --> 00:11:04.140
Hey! Stop them!

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:06.810
Th-They aren't stopping!

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:13.290
Hort! Kudo!

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:17.680
Are you okay, Saybil?

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:22.420
Oh. Look here.

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:27.040
No escort today!

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.720
My dear Ludens!

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:34.230
Clean up!

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:46.890
If such an easy task gets me a 
peek at <i>The Grimoire of Zero</i>,

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:48.530
then it's not even a question.

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:50.480
Right, my dear Ludens?

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:56.410
What's this?

00:11:57.460 --> 00:11:59.180
H-Help me.

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:05.200
My goodness. This is an unexpected find.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.880
How is the Tyrant here?

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:14.150
Hell if I know! But we're rescuing 
Saybil no matter who we have to fight.

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:15.710
It's moving!

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.840
Quiet! Just do it already!

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:19.190
Full power!

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:20.210
Okay.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.510
No incantation?

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:39.060
I see you've improved since last time.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:45.950
Please don't move. I can probably 
kill you in an instant.

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:51.870
What's this?

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.500
The third-rate servant.

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:57.800
Why art thou sleeping out here?

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:01.760
Why <i>was</i> I sleeping out here?

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:03.510
Art thou drunk?

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:08.510
No. I was about to have the kids 
take me to an empty house,

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:12.020
when that Uls fellow there showed up...

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:16.140
He said something about 
Saybil being abducted...

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.690
I tried to stop the kids 
from going after him.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.820
But then I...

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:25.110
Thou wert put to sleep, with magic.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:26.820
So then...

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:29.830
Oh crap! No!

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:34.070
What hast thou so flustered? 
'Tis <i>thy</i> trap, is it not?

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:37.580
Thou camest all the way out to this village.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:42.620
Thy plan was to cause an incident and 
observe whether we could resolve it.

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:44.480
As a sort of test, yes?

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:50.470
My ducklings assuredly felt wary of you.

00:13:52.110 --> 00:13:56.960
You don't think I might be trying 
to actually do something to Saybil?

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.480
Sorena wouldn't approve.

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:04.180
So, what is the issue?

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:06.490
I used the Tyrant.

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:08.360
Thou didst <i>what</i>?!

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:10.650
Then ya shoulda

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:15.680
killed me just now.

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:17.870
In combat...

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:20.750
Sayb!

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:20.750
Saybil!

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:25.840
whoever hesitates loses!

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:31.660
If ya ain't prepared to kill 
when ya have the chance,

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:35.390
it don't matter how strong 
your weapon is. It's useless.

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:38.640
I'd say this is within acceptable limits.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:41.650
Seein' as how ya can fix it all with magic.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:51.090
The Mask?

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:52.480
Bastard!

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:56.420
Didn't you leave the village?

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:58.160
I'm impressed you knew.

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:00.070
I came back.

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:10.440
My mouse made a big fuss about 
a pest entering the village.

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:15.180
Now I can finally see.

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:19.580
Don't worry. I'll take you alive.

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:21.780
There is so much information

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:23.400
to glean from you.

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:32.880
This is within acceptable limits, yes?

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:35.380
Since it can be fixed with magic.

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:40.080
Fighting the Mask in the forest at 
night is too big of a disadvantage.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:43.830
Plus you have reinforcements 
coming. I give up.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:50.680
See. I knew the priest would be here.

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:52.470
Quit grumbling, Mercenary.

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:55.790
If we hadn't raced here,

00:15:55.790 --> 00:16:00.730
our blood-starved priest might 
have julienned our assailant.

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:04.730
Looks like he's already 
been given a rough chop.

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:09.520
That is quite a way to speak 
when you two arrived late.

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:11.490
Hold it, hold it hold it!

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:13.690
You barbarians!

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:17.000
'Tis shameful to gang up 
on and bully the weak!

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:20.320
He took out all the students.

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:23.460
The Tyrant is tougher than I thought.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.210
Oh? So you two know him?

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:31.830
Depending on your answer,

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:36.720
we may be send your head back to the 
Mooncaller Witch at the Academy.

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:46.560
Look, the deal with the Tyrant was 
he would be spared the death penalty

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:50.980
if he could bring at least one 
student back to the Academy.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:55.990
In other words, this wasn't 
a test for the students.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:17:00.520
It was an inspection of the 
village's ability to protect them.

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:03.000
That's why he set the Tyrant loose,

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:08.870
but the students were wary of Holdem, 
who was obviously suspicious.

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:12.760
They removed him from the 
fight as soon as it started,

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:17.760
thus he was unable to restrain 
the Tyrant's excessive violence,

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:20.760
and he was late to arrive.

00:17:21.210 --> 00:17:22.550
Are you incompetent?

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:23.770
What are ya, incompetent?

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:27.770
Yes. I'm incompetent 
and a third-rate servant.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:30.740
It does no good to blame the dog.

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:33.810
If the Tyrant's aim had been murder,

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:36.210
the students would all have been killed.

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:40.010
We have no choice but to recognize

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:45.680
that this inspection fully exposed the 
weakness of the village's defenses.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:51.920
We were just short on hands this time 
because of the Remnant of Disaster.

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:55.850
More accurate to say we lack fighting power.

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:57.730
If it were just this village, 
it would be one thing,

00:17:57.730 --> 00:18:01.430
but if we try to protect the surrounding 
ones as well, we cannot attend to it all.

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:06.750
The towns around us are just 
getting dragged into our mess.

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:09.190
We can't just leave 'em in the lurch.

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:14.890
If witches bring extra danger and 
then do nothing to protect people,

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:17.900
the village may only worsen 
the reputation of witches.

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:21.620
Um, might I be permitted to say somethin—

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:22.940
Keep quiet.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.410
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:18:22.940 --> 00:18:24.410
Incompetence is contagious.

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:27.910
Don't bully him so. Well, let's hear it.

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:33.440
If you need more fighting power, 
please feel free to make use of him.

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:38.930
H-Hold up! That wasn't the deal!

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:44.440
Once I succeeded, my death sentence 
was supposed to be commuted—

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:45.930
You didn't succeed!

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:48.310
If you want to live, zip it!

00:18:56.090 --> 00:18:57.940
No way!

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:01.700
No way! Nuh-uh! Absolutely opposed!

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:04.790
He betrayed the Church, right?

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:07.960
Someone like that will betray us next!

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.580
You betrayed the Church, too.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:14.960
Kudo, why do you always say the 
thing someone least wants to hear?

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:18.460
The Tyrant tried to kill us!

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.560
You're telling me to forgive him?

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:22.840
It's better to execute him!

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:26.190
You need not forgive him, antlered girl.

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:31.400
If you desire revenge, I won't condemn you.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.730
However, there is one 
thing you must remember.

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:39.510
Witch hunts are revenge for 
witches' past wrongdoings.

00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:45.740
Those very wrongdoings are why witches 
continue to be regarded with suspicion.

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:47.780
The peace between the Church and witches...

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:52.760
Those whose loved ones were killed by 
witches find it difficult to accept.

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:54.250
I'm sure <i>you</i> understand their feelings.

00:19:55.080 --> 00:20:00.130
That is the very reason the anti-witch 
faction hires people like the Tyrant.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:05.140
The Tyrant has been ordered to serve 
this village to atone for his sins.

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:11.240
You must consider the purpose and 
significance of executing him now.

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:18.650
But the Tyrant has killed 
lots of innocent people, too.

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:21.390
The same is true of me.

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:26.760
I killed anybody the Church ordered me to.

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:28.530
Will you execute me as well?

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:29.840
B-But tha—

00:20:29.840 --> 00:20:31.290
You can't!

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:34.790
You can't execute the father!

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:37.910
He's not the same as the Tyrant.

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:44.770
Well, my dear Ludens is known as the witch 
eater and has taken the lives of many witches.

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:49.560
If one of their relatives comes for me, 
I have no right to complain.

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:53.810
No way! It's obviously not right 
for you to be killed, Professor!

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:59.600
What, so anyone you like is a good person 
no matter how many people they've killed?

00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:02.830
So you're fine with this?

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:06.070
As long as he's on our side.

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:08.280
He can't be trusted to be on our side!

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:10.080
He might attack us!

00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:13.690
If he does, we can just kill him then.

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:16.710
You'll be able to take him 
out for sure next time.

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:20.610
But what if he attacks 
Sayb while I'm not around?

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:21.960
Sayb will be killed!

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:24.340
Sorry for not being reliable.

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:26.830
That's not what I was saying.

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:30.970
Fine. This is a pain in the butt,
 so let's just execute him.

00:21:31.190 --> 00:21:33.210
You love to take arguments to extremes.

00:21:34.130 --> 00:21:34.910
Argh!

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:36.560
Ugh!

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:39.480
Fine! I'll monitor him, then!

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:46.740
We'll have him live in this bar, 
so Mr. Mercenary can monitor him.

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:50.400
And when I monitor him, 
I'll work his butt off.

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:52.990
Excuse me? He's gonna live in my bar?!

00:21:57.560 --> 00:22:00.000
Hort, you made a painful decision.

00:22:00.690 --> 00:22:04.010
I mean, after what everyone said...

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:08.010
You determined that letting the 
Tyrant live would be best,

00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:11.380
and you put your own feelings aside.

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:16.100
'Tis a feat even adults 
struggle to accomplish.

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:23.180
Professor Los!

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:10.010
<b>Next Episode  "A Stone Cast into the Pond"</b>

00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:57.620
Now this is exciting!

00:23:57.620 --> 00:24:01.870
If his memories return, then will 
his romance with Hort progress?

00:24:01.870 --> 00:24:03.960
Next episode: "A Stone Cast Into the Pond."

00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:07.840
I think I might like Professor Los.

00:24:09.340 --> 00:24:09.960
Excuse me?
